# Stoa attribution-advisory — PRINCIPAL identity allow-list.
# One accepted name or email per line ('#' comments + blanks ignored).
# The attribution-advisory skill's SECONDARY check compares NEW author-like
# field VALUES (added in a diff, outside vendored paths) against this list;
# a value not on the list is REPORTED for review in the advisory report.
# It is NEVER blocked or denied — the advisory is report-only. This is the
# SKILL'S CONFIG, not an author field of any repo artifact. Widen it when a
# legit PRINCIPAL identity is missing. An ABSENT or EMPTY list SKIPS the
# SECONDARY check (PRIMARY still runs, name-agnostic). Seeded from the
# target's global git identity + any --principal-name passed at install.
